#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:1
msgid "llvm-nm - list LLVM bitcode and object file's symbol table"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:6
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:8
msgid "{program}`llvm-nm` \\[*options*\\] \\[*filenames...*\\]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:10
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:12
msgid ""
"The {program}`llvm-nm` utility lists the names of symbols from LLVM bitcode "
"files, object files, and archives. Each symbol is listed along with some "
"simple information about its provenance. If no filename is specified, *a."
"out* is used as the input. If *-* is used as a filename, {program}`llvm-nm` "
"will read a file from its standard input stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:18
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-nm`'s default output format is the traditional BSD {program}"
"`nm` output format. Each such output record consists of an (optional) 8-"
"digit hexadecimal address, followed by a type code character, followed by a "
"name, for each symbol. One record is printed per line; fields are separated "
"by spaces. When the address is omitted, it is replaced by 8 spaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:24
msgid ""
"The supported type code characters are as follows. Where both lower and "
"upper-case characters are listed for the same meaning, a lower-case "
"character represents a local symbol, whilst an upper-case character "
"represents a global (external) symbol:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:29
msgid "`a`, `A`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:31
msgid "Absolute symbol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:33
msgid "`b`, `B`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:35
msgid "Uninitialized data (bss) object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:37
msgid "`C`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:39
msgid "Common symbol. Multiple definitions link together into one definition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:41
msgid "`d`, `D`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:43
msgid "Writable data object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:45
msgid "`i`, `I`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:47
msgid "COFF: .idata symbol or symbol in a section with IMAGE_SCN_LNK_INFO set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:49
msgid "`n`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:51
msgid "ELF: local symbol from non-alloc section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:53
msgid "COFF: debug symbol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:55
msgid "`N`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:57
msgid "ELF: debug section symbol, or global symbol from non-alloc section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:59
msgid "`s`, `S`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:61
msgid "COFF: section symbol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:63
msgid ""
"Mach-O: absolute symbol or symbol from a section other than \\_\\_TEXT_EXEC "
"\\_\\_text, \\_\\_TEXT \\_\\_text, \\_\\_DATA \\_\\_data, or \\_\\_DATA "
"\\_\\_bss."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:66
msgid "`r`, `R`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:68
msgid "Read-only data object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:70
msgid "`t`, `T`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:72
msgid "Code (text) object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:74
msgid "`u`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:76
msgid "ELF: GNU unique symbol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:78
msgid "`U`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:80
msgid "Named object is undefined in this file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:82
msgid "`v`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:84
msgid ""
"ELF: Undefined weak object. It is not a link failure if the object is not "
"defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:87
msgid "`V`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:89
msgid ""
"ELF: Defined weak object symbol. This definition will only be used if no "
"regular definitions exist in a link. If multiple weak definitions and no "
"regular definitions exist, one of the weak definitions will be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:93
msgid "`w`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:95
msgid ""
"Undefined weak symbol other than an ELF object symbol. It is not a link "
"failure if the symbol is not defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:98
msgid "`W`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:100
msgid ""
"Defined weak symbol other than an ELF object symbol. This definition will "
"only be used if no regular definitions exist in a link. If multiple weak "
"definitions and no regular definitions exist, one of the weak definitions "
"will be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:104
msgid "`-`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:106
msgid "Mach-O: N_STAB symbol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:108
msgid "`?`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:110
msgid "Something unrecognizable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:112
msgid ""
"Because LLVM bitcode files typically contain objects that are not considered "
"to have addresses until they are linked into an executable image or "
"dynamically compiled \"just-in-time\", {program}`llvm-nm` does not print an "
"address for any symbol in an LLVM bitcode file, even symbols which are "
"defined in the bitcode file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:118
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:124
msgid "Use BSD output format. Alias for `--format=bsd`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:128
msgid ""
"Specify the type of XCOFF object file, ELF object file, or IR object file "
"input from command line or from archive files that llvm-nm should examine. "
"The mode must be one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:132
msgid "32"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:133
msgid "Process only 32-bit object files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:135
msgid "64"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:136
msgid "Process only 64-bit object files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:138
msgid "32_64"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:139
msgid "Process both 32-bit and 64-bit object files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:141
msgid "any"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:142
msgid "Process all the supported object files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:144
msgid ""
"On AIX OS, the default is to process 32-bit object files only and to ignore "
"64-bit objects. The can be changed by setting the OBJECT_MODE environment "
"variable. For example, OBJECT_MODE=64 causes {program}`llvm-nm` to process "
"64-bit objects and ignore 32-bit objects. The -X flag overrides the "
"OBJECT_MODE variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:150
msgid ""
"On other operating systems, the default is to process all object files: the "
"OBJECT_MODE environment variable is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:155
msgid "Show all symbols, even those usually suppressed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:159
msgid "Print only symbols defined in this file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:163
msgid "Demangle symbol names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:167
msgid "Display dynamic symbols instead of normal symbols."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:171
msgid ""
"Print sorted symbols with their visibility (if applicable), with duplicates "
"removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:176
msgid ""
"Print only symbols whose definitions are external; that is, accessible from "
"other files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:181
msgid ""
"Select an output format; *format* may be *sysv*, *posix*, *darwin*, *bsd* or "
"*just-symbols*. The default is *bsd*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-nm.md:187
